ufac-s: n!, for n from 0 to 6.
Cells 84-98. To call it, load n into the accumulator and JMP 84.
It returns n! in the accumulator.
It overwrites its own cells and cell 99.
Size 15 cells. It runs at most 7 instructions, 7.0 on average, counted from cell 84 to the return jump in cell 98.
Exact over the domain; outside it, n reads past the table.

cell  contents   notes
 84     296      ADD 96   cells 84-88: build CLA 89 + n in cell 97, copy the return jump from cell 99 into cell 98, and jump to the load
 85     697      STO 97
 86     199      CLA 99
 87     698      STO 98
 88     897      JMP 97
 89     001      data: the table of factorials, 0! to 6!
 90     001
 91     002
 92     006
 93     024
 94     120
 95     720
 96     189      data: CLA of the table's first cell, an instruction the routine copies and changes
 97     000      set on every call: CLA of n!, which loads it into the accumulator
 98     000      set on every call: the jump back to the caller
